comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T20:22:44.377Z",codex-root,"GitHub issue: https://github.com/unbraind/homeassistant-cli/issues/79"
  "2026-07-31T20:44:17.331Z",codex-root,Repaired exactly four affected history streams while preserving current items. Cache-cleared strict validation now reports 67 checked items and zero mismatches; clean-worktree auto-release dry-run completed full verification plus npx and bunx tarball smoke tests without publishing. Issue remains active until hosted PR checks prove fresh-runner parity.
  "2026-07-31T21:05:24.040Z",codex-root,"Hosted fresh-runner proof passed on PR 80 exact implementation head 5c6ebb04186d7c02c7f94c2bbb8f942dfa3ea544. PM integrity,Bun and Node quality,exact coverage,changelog,package smoke,CodeQL,dependency audit,Trivy,history scan,and commit policy were green; GitHub issue 79 closed with merge 8a0c573248c039bc4732c4f2f6ed1dac40752023."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T20:22:44.377Z",codex-root,The initial cached local validation was a false negative; pm gc --scope runtime made the checkout reproduce the clean-runner failure.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T20:22:44.377Z",codex-root,"Release integrity checks must invalidate derived history-drift caches when item/history content changes, or clean-runner parity can diverge."
